Z||000000||Alex11||06-25-2001||01:43 AM||||I am six foot five, can i fit in a fiero and drive it comfortably?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||06-25-2001||01:44 AM||||ubetcha! Plenty of room in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MODIFIE||06-25-2001||03:42 AM||||set in one and see that would be the best way to see if its the car for you good luck||||reg||10
Z||000003||84Bill||06-25-2001||08:40 AM||||6'1" here and I have room to spare, infact the seat is 1 notch from the rear.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-25-2001||09:14 AM||||you'll be comfortable driving the car - even more so in the passenger side<P>but its gonna be a long way back when you have to get out and stand up - the fiero door handles will be just below your kneecaps when you stand next to the car.<P> thats what we need to do. find the tallest person around and get photos of our cars with him standing next to it.<P> 1/2 scale model?! no thats my Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||06-25-2001||10:02 AM||||I'm 6'3" and about 240 lbs.  I fit with no problem and room left over. Ken is right--getting out can be a long ways up!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||14
Z||000006||fierobaby||06-25-2001||11:48 AM||||I found being 5'3" is a great height for the car I can get in pretty easy and get out easy although the seat has to be almost the whole way up!  :-)<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||terryk||06-25-2001||02:53 PM||||I'm 6' 4" and if I sit straight up, my head would hit the roof if the sunroof wasn't there. Also, on a manual trans car, there is no place to rest your left foot. The automatic is nicer. Overall, the leg room is fine otherwise.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||06-25-2001||04:43 PM||||I'm 6'2" and about 240# (I think that would be somewhere around 892kg? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and I fit fine.  My left foot rests on the dead pedal with room to spare (33" inseam).  And everyone else is absolutely correct...it's a heck of a long way up when you exit.  Just remember..."Fall in, Roll out!"<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000009||87FieroGTx||06-25-2001||08:11 PM|||| I'm 6'3" 270 and fit fine, I'v even got in with my Football pads on and didnt have any problems.||||reg||1
Z||000010||hyhy4u||06-25-2001||08:49 PM||||Im 6"4' and i dont have any problems, the only problem you'll get is all the crap you will get from people telling you how stupid you are that you bought such a small car for being such a big guy...but just tell them to get in the pass. side and when they cant touch the end they will shut up!||||reg||1
Z||000011||stimpy||06-25-2001||09:52 PM||||6'6" here, 280#. I fit, but I don't think you could get much bigger thn this and be able to fit.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex11||06-26-2001||02:17 AM||||So there is no dead pedal on the manual transmission cars?  No place for the left foot to rest?  Is that what I am hearing?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||no_rice||06-26-2001||02:56 AM||||im 6'6 and about 225 and i steal my friends fiero from him (seanh) and i fit comfortably in it||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||06-26-2001||05:06 AM||||I'm 6'2" tall, though I weigh ~170lbs.<P>I fit fine, but I find cars with T-tops or sunroof to offer about an inch of headroom.<P>Hardtop cars are, ah, borderline.<P>But Fieros are actually roomier than most cars.  I don't fit in a honda accord. <BR>And I tried to get into a dodge caravan the other day, almost killed myself. then sat in back.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000015||stimpy||06-26-2001||10:41 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex11:<BR><B>So there is no dead pedal on the manual transmission cars?  No place for the left foot to rest?  Is that what I am hearing?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is a dead pedal on the drivers side. I don't know what that terryk was talking about. I think he likes to stretch out.<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
